# Mounting NTFS Drives with Write Support

Linux includes read-only NTFS support in the kernel by default. For write access,
you have two options depending on your kernel version...

## Option 1: ntfs-3g (FUSE-based, all kernels)

The `ntfs-3g` driver works via FUSE and is available on any Linux version.

```bash
# Install
sudo apt install ntfs-3g       # Debian/Ubuntu
sudo dnf install ntfs-3g       # Fedora
sudo pacman -S ntfs-3g         # Arch

# Mount manually
sudo mount -t ntfs-3g /dev/sdb1 /mnt/data

# Verify write access
touch /mnt/data/test.txt && echo "write OK"
```

